# Gitignored files that Claude Code copies into each new worktree it creates.
# `.gitignore` syntax; only files that match AND are gitignored are copied, so a
# tracked file can never be duplicated by a pattern here.
#
# A worktree is a fresh checkout, so without this a new one has no environment at
# all and every stage fails on a missing key. See docs/project/worktrees.md.
#
# Deliberately NOT here: `.env.prod`. An agent in a worktree must not be able to
# deploy, and `npm run deploy` refuses a `worktree-*` branch by name as well —
# scripts/deploy-checks.ts, `deployBranchProblem`.
#
# One trap if you add a pattern later: a `**/`-prefixed pattern does not reach
# into a wholly-gitignored directory unless the first name after `**/` is one of
# the names in that directory's path. Name the directory instead —
# `vendor/**/config.json`, not `**/config.json`.
.env.local
.env
